 "findings": {
  "regression": {
   "headline": "expr::bvar_in_range - a COMPLETE five-link chain, the first computing chain, 21 non-vacuous marker lines - loses links 1/2b at the guarded tip: verdict agreed->unsupported, flip gone at BOTH levels",
   "lost_agreed_O3": [
    "env::ext_instance::PRIORITY_BYTES",
    "expr::bvar_in_range",
    "expr::types::FVarId::SENTINEL_RANGE_START",
    "tc::heartbeat_profiler::types::clamp_u32"
   ],
   "new_verdict_detail": "unsupported: comparator(built): constant outside fragment: OpaqueScalar { width: 32|64, signed: false }",
   "culprit": "trust 2239682f9c (fix(trust-ir): break the CTFE query cycles): the ctfe_reentrancy freeze declines forced const-evaluation of LOCAL mir::Const::Unevaluated operands during mir_built lowering, so local associated constants reach the comparator as OpaqueScalar; the frozen oracle (709a7794) then refuses them - fail-closed and loud, so agreed drops rather than anything being admitted wrong",
   "direction": "the refusal is the fail-closed direction and is correct oracle behaviour; the fix is a PRODUCER build item (evaluate non-cyclic local consts, or carry their identity), never a comparator relaxation",
   "not_the_oracle_guard": "the refuse-more Rvalue::Ref guard (f429bb245c) fired on NOTHING: zero other rows moved, and wave-MC's class is untouched as its report predicted"
  },
  "instrument": {
   "sysrootcheck_is_not_sufficient": "the tip driver ICEs decoding the 2026-08-20 laneMV v12 sysroot (invalid enum variant tag while decoding StmtDebugInfo, expected 0..2, actual 15) because trust f24fdb2fdb added Statement.trust_modular_arith to the MIR encoding WITHOUT a METADATA_VERSION bump; seal_driver.sh sysrootcheck reports driver=12 sysroot=12 OK on that very pair. METADATA_VERSION equality is necessary, not sufficient; this lane proved its pair with a real optimized compile instead, and rebuilt the sysroot with the measured driver itself"
  }
 }
